  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the following sequence of reactions:\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0016_f1b6d2317941.png\"/><br/>\n11.25 mg of chlorobenzene will produce __________ $\\times 10^{-1} \\mathrm{mg}$ of product B .\n(Consider the reactions result in complete conversion.)\n[Given molar mass of $\\mathrm{C}, \\mathrm{H}, \\mathrm{O}, \\mathrm{N}$ and Cl as $12,1,16,14$ and $35.5 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ respectively]"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "93",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0016_39a7cb3a9dc1.png\"><br><img src=\"assets\\st0016_03b03ec44e03.png\"><br>\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{11.25 \\times 10^{-3}}{112.5}=\\frac{x \\times 10^{-1} \\times 10^{-3}}{93} \\\\ & x \\times 10^{-1}=93 \\times 0.1 \\\\ & x=93 \\mathrm{mg}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
